Sources/FirmDropCore/Authenticator.swift is a port of its
CryptUtils.authenticateBlock, and Sources/FirmDropCore/FUSClient.swift
follows its FUS client.

The bundled auth_param.dat file comes from the Bifrost repository at a
fixed commit and is verified by its SHA-256 checksum. It is fetched at
build time and is not stored in this source repository.

The app bundles a separate firmware installation executable:

Brokkr (https://github.com/Gabriel2392/brokkr-flash)
Copyright (c) 2026 Gabriel2392
Licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later (see Brokkr-LICENSE.txt).
Pinned commit: f7ae23067b4ee6c2e0211a1dee563f4be991cb4d.
Engine/main.cpp, Engine/compat.hpp, Engine/build.sh,
Engine/strict-mapping.patch, Engine/resume-session.patch,
Engine/download-list.patch and Engine/macos-sdk.patch are the FirmDrop
GPL-3.0-or-later adapter.
The Swift app communicates with this executable through process arguments
and stdout/stderr. It does not link to Brokkr.

Contents/Resources/flash-engine-source.tar.gz contains the complete
corresponding sources, including the adapter, its patches,
build instructions, dependencies and their licenses. Brokkr-NOTICES.txt
contains the upstream dependency notices. Dependencies include spdlog, fmt,
function2, LZ4, xxHash and MD5; their license files remain in the source bundle.

The app bundles the adb executable from the Android SDK Platform-Tools:

Android Debug Bridge (https://developer.android.com/tools/releases/platform-tools)
Copyright The Android Open Source Project
Version 37.0.1, downloaded from dl.google.com at build time and verified
by its SHA-256 checksum. It is used only to request a reboot to Download
mode and is invoked as a separate process.
adb-NOTICE.txt contains the Platform-Tools license notices.
